WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.290
Today is about a whole story. What happened first, what happened then, and what happened last.

2
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.356
These are today's two pages.

3
00:00:07.806 --> 00:00:12.330
On the first page, three sentences tell a little story. But they are mixed up.

4
00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:16.189
Your child reads all three. Then ask: what happened first?

5
00:00:16.639 --> 00:00:22.033
Your child writes one, two and three in the boxes. Then reads the story again, in order.

6
00:00:22.483 --> 00:00:26.422
That last read is the check. In the right order, the story makes sense.

7
00:00:26.872 --> 00:00:31.038
Job two is for your child alone. Two more little stories to put in order.

8
00:00:31.488 --> 00:00:34.406
Then turn to the story. Your child reads it to you.

9
00:00:34.856 --> 00:00:38.335
Now cover the story with your hand, and say: tell it back to me.

10
00:00:38.785 --> 00:00:44.275
There are three pictures under the story. First, then, last. They help your child keep the order.

11
00:00:44.725 --> 00:00:48.814
Your child’s own words are fine. They do not have to be the words of the book.

12
00:00:49.264 --> 00:00:55.355
If a part is missing, do not tell it. Uncover the story, and say: read it again. What do you see?

13
00:00:55.805 --> 00:00:58.972
Then let your child tell the story to someone else in the family.
